//   id      never change it: saved chats store levels under it
//   label   the name in the panel
//   cue     what it covers
//   words   words in a message that call for it ('|' between, '*' ends a stem). They also count as practice,
//           so keep them to things someone does with the skill, not things that merely come up
//   prompt  (optional) the wording sent, when the label alone could be misread
//   when    (optional) what else calls for it, space-separated: seems (the player's feelings were read last reply),
//           mind (a Mind setting), power (control shifted), feel:<mood category>, dyn:<dynamic group>,
//           cat:<fact category>, fact:<id>. These light it without counting as practice.
//   bad     (optional) ways a minus level can show, '|' between. Two are offered to Claude as examples, never a
//           script, picked by the reply number so the fumble changes from reply to reply.
//   cue is sent in full only while the skill is lit, so it can cover every way the skill gets used.
